<title>FRANCE: U.S. main origin for Jan-May 97 Paris air imports.</title>
<headline>U.S. main origin for Jan-May 97 Paris air imports.</headline>
<text>
<p>July 8, Reuter - The U.S. was the principal country of origin for import traffic handled at the Paris airports in January-May 1997, Paris airport authority (ADP), figures show.</p>
<p>In Jan-May import traffic to the Paris  airports, Charles de Gaulle and Orly, totalled 221,614 tonnes, an increase of 3.7 percent on the same period last year, Aeroports de Paris ADP figures show.</p>
<p>The top 20 countries for ADP imports in Jan-May, with percentage change on January-May 1996 were:</p>
<p>	Origin	Jan-May '97  Jan-May '96</p>
<p>			    tonnes    Pct Change</p>
<p>   1. United States   59,717    down   3.6</p>
<p>   2. India	     10,593    down   7.2</p>
<p>   3. Japan	     10,511	up  46.0</p>
<p>   4. Canada	     9,396    down  19.0</p>
<p>   5. U.K.		 9,087	up  34.0</p>
<p>   6. Hong Kong	  8,012	up  12.9</p>
<p>   7. Germany	    6,654	up  14.9</p>
<p>   8. Thailand	   5,551	up  33.9</p>
<p>   9. Italy		4,681    down   8.6</p>
<p>  10. Fr.W Indies	4,544	up   7.3</p>
<p>  11. Senegal	    4,214	up  11.5</p>
<p>  12. Singapore	  3,925	up  89.6</p>
<p>  13. Kenya		3,709    down  21.0</p>
<p>  14. Morocco	    3,005    down  22.7</p>
<p>  15. China		2,908	up  66.8</p>
<p>  16. Argentine	  2,904	up   0.6</p>
<p>  17. Brazil	     2,869	up  26.9</p>
<p>  18. Egypt		2,849	up  35.2</p>
<p>  19. Korea		2,684	up  24.5</p>
<p>  20. Mauritius	  2,490	up  23.0</p>
<p>- Reuters Air Cargo Service Tel+ 44 171 542 7706 Fax +5017 - www.racs.com</p>
